# =============================================================
# .dockerignore — files Docker must NOT copy into the image
#
# The Dockerfile runs "COPY . ." which copies the whole project
# folder. Anything listed here is skipped. This matters for
# privacy: without it, your real API keys (.env), your database
# and all your videos would be baked into the image, and anyone
# who got hold of the image could read them.
#
# Secrets and data reach the container another way instead:
# docker-compose.yml passes .env in at start-up and mounts the
# data folders from the server's disk.
# =============================================================

# --- Secrets ---
.env

# --- Data (mounted from the server's disk at run time) ---
output/
cache/
data/
models/
recordings/
permissions/
shortsengine.db
*.db

# --- Not needed to run the app ---
.git/
.github/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
docs/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
